Okay, I know this subject has been done to death a few times over, but
I may have a new angle....

Pretty much everyone agrees that Gehennom is boring. A major component
of the boredom is that everybody hates the interminable mazes, and
we've discussed ad nauseum YANIs to change this. The best suggestions
I've heard are 1) decreasing the number of levels, perhaps to nine,
and perhaps emulating in some degree the circles of Dante's Inferno;
and 2) making the "default" form of the Gehennom levels something like
a more open version of the Mines, so that each level would be
something like a dark, irregularly shaped Bigroom.

So much for proposed changes to the physical layout of Gehennom. The
other problem with Gehennom is the fact that most characters will be,
and more or less need to be, essentially ascension-ready by the time
they descend below the Castle. It's pretty difficult to do both the
Castle and the Quest  without all your resistances, good AC,
reasonably good hp, etc. That's basically what you need to ascend.
Whatever items you're lacking can be made up with the Castle wand, as
well as being able to enchant your gear up the wazoo. You need a means
to cross water to get past Medusa (well, not really, but who's going
to descend beyond the Castle without a for-sure way to get *back*
across the water on their way back up?) so that takes care of
Juiblex's Swamp. So basically, past the Castle, most characters will
be unstoppable killing machines, and the rest of the game (at least up
to the Planes) is just going through the motions to grind it out.

What makes the early game interesting is the quest to gain the
necessary intrinsics and gear to be able to survive. Here's my idea:

What if there were another set of intrinsics that were only necessary
in Gehennom and were only possible to get in Gehennom?

It doesn't have to be intrinsics; it could be some other kind of gear
or magical items; just something. Think of it. All of a sudden,
there's something to look for besides the downstairs (ok, and the
stairs to Vlad's and the Wizard's Portal and the VS). All of a sudden,
there's something you need that you can't prepare for before you hit
Gehennom.

I'm not sure what, exactly. Maybe you need to cross superheated lava,
and levitation, waterwalking, fireproofing, and fire resistance won't
do it. Maybe you need to dig through an otherwise undiggable wall, and
need some special tool to do it. Maybe some resistances/item
properties wouldn't be a basic toggle; they'd be treated more like
Magic Cancellation. (The relationship between MR and MC gives an idea
of what I'm looking for; maybe you need fire cancellation, cold
cancellation, etc.) Maybe all cloaks start at MC 1 and you need a
special wand or scroll to raise it up to MC 3, one which doesn't exist
outside Gehennom.

What say ye? Any ideas?
